<!--
  The package-identity publishers: the ONE build-time home
  (docs/goal/architecture/installers/windows.md § Package identity for FaunaApp.exe).

  MSIX binds a package to its signing certificate by requiring Identity/@Publisher to
  equal the certificate's Subject DN exactly, and the publisher feeds the package
  family name, so a copy that drifts is silently another app. So every consumer
  reads it from here, never a copy (scripts/_windows_package_identity.py parses this
  file):

    - the store-package build script, the one packer of both full-MSIX channels,
      defaults a dev build's publisher to FaunaPackagePublisher;
    - the e2e harness registers its dev packages under it
      (tests/e2e-unified/helpers/taskbar_badge.py).

  FaunaPackagePublisher is the DEV self-sign DN, which is what every local build and
  e2e run uses. The Store channel's production publisher is NOT here: it is the
  Partner Center identity (installers/windows.md § Identity & coexistence), passed to
  the store build as its own publisher argument; only the store build's dev default
  comes from here.

  FaunaDirectProductionPublisher is the DIRECT-DOWNLOAD package's production
  publisher (installers/windows.md § Direct download, 5): the exact subject string
  of the certificate that signs Fauna.msixbundle, read off the signer before the
  first signed release and never changed after it (the package family hashes it, so
  another string is another app that cannot update this one). EMPTY until the signer
  is chosen; `just windows-direct-package production` refuses while it is. No
  Condition: the string is recorded here, in the goal doc and in
  installer/official-apps.json, which must agree, so nothing overrides it at build
  time. A dev direct build packs with the dev DN above.

  Pinned by tests/e2e-unified/tests/platform/windows/test_package_identity_publisher.py.
-->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <FaunaPackagePublisher Condition="'$(FaunaPackagePublisher)' == ''">CN=Fauna Social (Dev)</FaunaPackagePublisher>
    <FaunaDirectProductionPublisher></FaunaDirectProductionPublisher>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
